1231:  # Floor under the same drain for cron jobs and api_server (/v1) runs
1232-  # (seconds). Default 30.
1233-  # restart_drain_timeout above is written for chat turns, which are cheap to
1234-  # interrupt: the user is told the gateway is restarting and the session
1235-  # resumes on their next message. A cron run has no such safety net — it is
1236-  # recorded in jobs.json as a permanent failure, nobody is waiting on it, and
1237-  # a recurring job simply skips to its next schedule. So in-flight cron work
1238-  # gets its own grace window instead of inheriting the 0 above, and so do
1239:  # api_server (/v1) runs: an interrupted /v1 run fails its waiting caller.
1240-  # Clamped at runtime to the shutdown-watchdog leash (restart_drain_timeout
1241-  # + 60s) minus teardown headroom, so values past ~50s need a matching
1242-  # TimeoutStopSec bump to take effect. Set 0 to opt out and drain cron and
